1
00:00:00,735 --> 00:00:04,585
A robot is preparing fruit. Is its gripper safe to use?

2
00:00:06,385 --> 00:00:09,860
First, the left gripper touches a contaminated tray.

3
00:00:11,385 --> 00:00:14,285
It then carries contamination to the spoon handle.

4
00:00:16,385 --> 00:00:19,473
The robot washes both grippers, but not the spoon.

5
00:00:19,785 --> 00:00:21,772
Its handle stays contaminated.

6
00:00:25,385 --> 00:00:28,888
The assistant returns the spoon, contaminating the clean right

7
00:00:28,898 --> 00:00:29,860
gripper again.

8
00:00:32,385 --> 00:00:36,262
The fruit-handling plan must change. First, the robot puts down

9
00:00:36,272 --> 00:00:36,973
the spoon.

10
00:00:38,385 --> 00:00:42,450
User priorities can favor different treatments. We demonstrate

11
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:44,922
washing with water and wiping with paper.

12
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:51,835
After treatment, the robot resumes placing fruit.

13
00:00:53,385 --> 00:00:56,888
Planning must decide what to treat, when, and at what resource

14
00:00:56,898 --> 00:00:57,535
cost.

15
00:01:00,385 --> 00:01:03,800
The benchmark formalizes this choice as washing or replacing the

16
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:08,848
contact pad. User priorities determine the preferred safe continuation.

17
00:01:11,385 --> 00:01:15,185
HygieneRoboBench tests household planning under contact history,

18
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,447
user priorities, and new events.

19
00:01:18,802 --> 00:01:24,842
Our 624 instances form 134 task families, covering five activity

20
00:01:24,852 --> 00:01:27,052
groups and seven household areas.

21
00:01:28,285 --> 00:01:32,610
Figure three shows three views of these same 624 instances:

22
00:01:33,148 --> 00:01:37,137
activity groups, construction designs, and difficulty. The rings

23
00:01:37,148 --> 00:01:40,960
partition the same dataset; they are not additional samples.

24
00:01:42,285 --> 00:01:47,050
Each task provides a request, physical observations, history, resources,

25
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:50,010
available events, and ordered user priorities.

26
00:01:50,618 --> 00:01:55,083
Under shared rules, planners return actions, objects, gripper assignments,

27
00:01:55,093 --> 00:01:58,568
and schedules, or an infeasible or undetermined judgment.

28
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:03,322
Controlled pairs change history, priorities, or event information,

29
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,735
keeping other task conditions fixed.

30
00:02:07,102 --> 00:02:09,539
Figure two shows how the benchmark is built.

31
00:02:09,852 --> 00:02:13,852
Household activities and hygiene guidance feed five shared registries,

32
00:02:14,089 --> 00:02:17,077
which define the rules used to construct each task.

33
00:02:20,752 --> 00:02:25,829
Tasks adapt BEHAVIOR-1K activities. Published studies and public-health

34
00:02:25,839 --> 00:02:29,729
guidance inform hygiene rules with explicit material and procedure

35
00:02:29,739 --> 00:02:30,739
requirements.

36
00:02:31,352 --> 00:02:34,979
In the fruit task, washing requires an empty gripper and treats

37
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:38,839
only its contact pad. The spoon stays separately tracked.

38
00:02:39,452 --> 00:02:43,064
Washing and replacement have abstract time and resource costs,

39
00:02:43,427 --> 00:02:46,152
giving planners a common basis for comparison.

40
00:02:47,385 --> 00:02:51,587
For general parameter construction, an LLM screens online time

41
00:02:51,597 --> 00:02:55,400
and supply estimates; reviewers check plausibility and relative

42
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,422
magnitudes.

43
00:02:57,052 --> 00:03:01,367
Washing saves spare parts. Replacement saves water but produces

44
00:03:01,377 --> 00:03:05,389
waste. User priorities determine the preferred safe option.

45
00:03:06,018 --> 00:03:10,456
Two reviewers check applicability, action conditions, and consistency;

46
00:03:10,693 --> 00:03:14,621
a third gives final review. Programs separately validate matched

47
00:03:14,631 --> 00:03:16,718
conditions and reference targets.

48
00:03:17,352 --> 00:03:21,529
The episode builder combines a base task with histories, priorities,

49
00:03:21,539 --> 00:03:25,827
and event information. Matched-condition checks, reference validation,

50
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:29,889
independent replay, and human review govern dataset admission.

51
00:03:32,702 --> 00:03:36,604
Independent of the planning solver, the evaluator replays history

52
00:03:36,614 --> 00:03:40,164
and checks goals, hygiene, timing, and resource limits.

53
00:03:40,785 --> 00:03:43,672
Holding the spoon violates the washing precondition.

54
00:03:43,972 --> 00:03:47,497
Putting it down first satisfies the empty-gripper requirement.

55
00:03:48,118 --> 00:03:52,421
The evaluator recomputes costs and compares them with private reference

56
00:03:52,431 --> 00:03:56,483
targets under the same priorities. Planners cannot access these

57
00:03:56,493 --> 00:03:57,293
targets.

58
00:03:57,918 --> 00:04:01,921
Safe resolution credits safe completion or correct infeasibility

59
00:04:01,931 --> 00:04:06,396
rejection. Optimal safe resolution also requires reference-optimal

60
00:04:06,406 --> 00:04:08,256
costs for submitted plans.

61
00:04:09,602 --> 00:04:14,254
We evaluate five language models, Rule-SAT, and Hygiene-NSP on

62
00:04:14,264 --> 00:04:16,777
the same 624 instances.

63
00:04:17,385 --> 00:04:23,000
Hygiene-NSP reaches 94.4 percent safe resolution and 90.4 percent

64
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:26,573
optimal safe resolution, the highest overall rates.

65
00:04:27,185 --> 00:04:33,550
DeepSeek produces 98 safe, nonoptimal plans. In 41, water or replacement

66
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:36,285
parts is the first nonoptimal cost dimension.

67
00:04:36,918 --> 00:04:40,381
All seven planners score lower as difficulty increases.

68
00:04:40,693 --> 00:04:44,996
Activity breakdowns reveal different strengths: Gemini leads cleaning

69
00:04:45,006 --> 00:04:45,831
and laundry.

70
00:04:47,168 --> 00:04:50,818
These fruit histories share physical conditions and priorities.

71
00:04:51,118 --> 00:04:55,233
Changing whether washing precedes spoon contact changes the contamination

72
00:04:55,243 --> 00:04:55,881
state.

73
00:04:56,518 --> 00:05:00,758
Prioritizing spare parts, the contaminated case needs washing before

74
00:05:00,768 --> 00:05:04,683
fruit handling. The clean case can continue directly after putting

75
00:05:04,693 --> 00:05:05,593
down the spoon.

76
00:05:06,818 --> 00:05:10,693
Swap the histories, keeping saved actions and timing fixed.

77
00:05:11,006 --> 00:05:15,821
Direct continuation becomes unsafe. Washing stays safe, but adds

78
00:05:15,831 --> 00:05:17,331
unnecessary treatment.

79
00:05:18,552 --> 00:05:22,289
As a control, histories differ on an unused side pad.

80
00:05:22,589 --> 00:05:26,989
Neither continuation touches it again. Outcomes stay unchanged.

81
00:05:28,218 --> 00:05:34,333
After relevant-history swaps, none of 1,699 originally safe, optimal

82
00:05:34,343 --> 00:05:40,583
replays retain both. All 1,288 irrelevant-history evaluations preserve

83
00:05:40,593 --> 00:05:41,606
their outcomes.

84
00:05:43,568 --> 00:05:47,933
Priority pairs instead fix history and action costs, testing whether

85
00:05:47,943 --> 00:05:51,306
plans adapt when users change their resource preferences.

86
00:05:51,918 --> 00:05:59,008
Hygiene-NSP succeeds on 234 of 268 general pairs and 24 of 25 ranking-flip

87
00:05:59,018 --> 00:06:01,031
pairs, leading both groups.

88
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:06,142
Event tests update history and context. Fifty relevant and fifty

89
00:06:06,152 --> 00:06:10,354
irrelevant instances assess safe, optimal continuation after new

90
00:06:10,364 --> 00:06:11,802
contact information.

91
00:06:12,418 --> 00:06:17,156
Hygiene-NSP reaches 88 and 92 percent optimal safe resolution.

92
00:06:17,456 --> 00:06:19,781
Gemini leads both event conditions.

93
00:06:21,735 --> 00:06:25,860
Hygiene-NSP grounds requests and priorities with a language model.

94
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:29,398
A trusted compiler checks the structured planning problem.

95
00:06:30,018 --> 00:06:34,996
History replay reconstructs hygiene states. CP-SAT jointly schedules

96
00:06:35,006 --> 00:06:38,218
treatment and service actions under user priorities.

97
00:06:38,852 --> 00:06:42,454
Optional state projection retains task-relevant information in

98
00:06:42,464 --> 00:06:46,364
a smaller representation, with full-state fallback when needed.

99
00:06:46,985 --> 00:06:52,062
Across 177 paired runs, local planning time improves by a median

100
00:06:52,072 --> 00:06:57,425
20.1 percent across families, excluding language-model calls. Status

101
00:06:57,435 --> 00:07:00,398
and cost agree in 175 pairs.

102
00:07:02,335 --> 00:07:06,375
HygieneRoboBench connects contact history, resource priorities,

103
00:07:06,385 --> 00:07:10,450
and event response: evaluating both safe completion and the right

104
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:11,910
safe choice for the user.

105
00:07:12,518 --> 00:07:16,656
Thank you for watching. Explore the benchmark on the project page.
